  "id": "COMPOUND:16577 - PROTEIN:812",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound (7S,8R,12R,19S,20S)-8-hydroxy-17-methoxy-7,15,19,20-tetramethyl-3,5,11-trioxapentacyclo[10.7.1.02,6.08,20.014,19]icos-16-ene-10,18-dione and 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that interact with this receptor. Specifically, the compound is associated with the Kappa-type opioid receptor, which is known to be a target of both Technetium Tc-99m sestamibi and Ginkgolide A, an analytical standard. Additionally, 3-Methylfentanyl, another compound linked to the Kappa-type opioid receptor, also targets 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C. These findings collectively indicate that the compound may interact with the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C through a mechanism involving the Kappa-type opioid receptor, suggesting a possible role in receptor activation or modulation. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, highlighting a potential functional relationship between the compound and the receptor, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and biological relevance.",
